1d:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-400 rounded-xl p-6 mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2","children":"What This Coursework Is"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-800 leading-relaxed","children":"IMPORTANT — this coursework is not a license and does not satisfy any state training requirement. In New York, a security guard completes an 8-hour pre-assignment course at a school approved by the Division of Criminal Justice Services (DCJS) before applying, registers with the NYS Department of State, Division of Licensing Services, completes 16 hours of on-the-job training within 90 days of starting work, and takes an 8-hour in-service course every year. Armed guard work also requires a New York pistol license, a 47-hour firearms course, and annual firearms training. Other states have their own requirements. No online course from a non-approved provider satisfies these, and this one does not claim to. Use it to arrive at approved training already understanding the material. Nothing here is legal advice — authority, use of force, and citizen's arrest are defined by state law and vary considerably."}]]}]
